      ":question/id": "cbe5a6ce-66c7-596b-b8a9-de22c81bf4bb",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{- 8 x^{3} + 2}{- 2 x^{4} + 2 x + 3}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=- 2 x^{4} + 2 x + 3.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=- 8 x^{3} + 2\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=(- 8 x^{3} + 2)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{- 8 x^{3} + 2}{- 2 x^{4} + 2 x + 3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{- 2 x^{4} + 2 x + 3}\\cdot (- 8 x^{3} + 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|- 2 x^{4} + 2 x + 3|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
